<h1>About Me</h1>

<p>
  I'm Alen, a full stack web developer based in Grand Rapids, Michigan, but if
  you caught me on a weekend, you're more likely to find me elbow deep in a
  3D printer or standing in a river than sitting at a keyboard. I like building
  things, physical or digital, and figuring out exactly how they work.
</p>

<h2>The Maker in Me</h2>
<p>
  I design and 3D print my own hardware, mostly things nobody makes quite the
  way I want them. My flagship project is a flipped GPU travel kit for the
  FormD T1 small form factor case, co-designed with a redditor from Sweden,
  he handled the CAD, I tested it against my own RTX 5090 and Ryzen 9950X3D
  build and gave feedback until it actually worked right. We released it free
  and non-commercial on Printables, no strings attached. I also designed an
  under-desk swivel mount for my Stream Deck, starting from a piece of tape
  holding it in place, then rebuilding it properly, first in Fusion 360, then
  teaching myself SolidWorks from scratch to redo it there too. I tend to
  iterate on things well past "good enough" until they match the exact
  picture in my head.
</p>

<h2>Fishing, and Where Fishédex Came From</h2>
<p>
  Fishing is genuinely one of my favorite things, fly fishing and bass
  fishing mostly, out on Michigan rivers like the Rogue. A friend I got into
  fishing kept texting me asking what species he'd just caught, over and
  over, until I finally decided to just build the answer instead of typing it
  out every time. That's how Fishédex started, a Pokémon-inspired fishing
  companion app that uses AI to identify fish species from a photo, with a
  manual fallback if the AI isn't sure either. It's still a passion project,
  not something I've launched publicly yet, but it's the one I'm proudest of,
  because it came from an actual problem, not a tutorial.
</p>

<h2>Content and Branding</h2>
<p>
  I create content under the name Sprout, technology videos, PC builds,
  undervolting experiments, hardware reviews, and a second channel called
  Troutcore dedicated to fishing. I designed both brand logos myself, all
  built around the same idea: minimalist, black and white, geometric, with
  a hidden symbol tied to the name buried in the shape. Sprout's leaf secretly
  forms an "S." Troutcore's trout hides a "T" in its stripes. Small details like that
  matter to me more than they probably should.
</p>

<h2>Also Building This Site</h2>
<p>
  Speaking of building things, this very site is one of them. I'm learning
  Ruby on Rails from the ground up, one small piece at a time, models,
  controllers, views, real debugging, no shortcuts. It's the same instinct
  that drives everything else I build: I'd rather understand how something
  actually works than just have it work.
</p>

<h2>Outside of All That</h2>
<p>
  When I'm not building or fishing, I'm probably gaming, or just chopping
  it up with friends. I guess it's probably important to mention that I am also
  married to the most beautiful and loving person I know. With whom I am
  soon to be welcoming our first baby to the world. I also spend an unreasonable
  amount of time tuning my own PC, undervolting, memory tuning, stability testing,
  mostly because I like knowing exactly what my hardware is actually capable of.
</p>
